From: MilkFlint <milkflint@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: keep counting txq schedule rounds after a
 blocked one

ieee80211_txq_schedule_start() sets the AC's round to 0 when the AC is
over its AQL budget (no txq is handed out), and the next start counted on
from there, so rounds restarted at 1 after every blocked one. A txq
served in an earlier round 1 then matched the new round at the head of
the list, and ieee80211_next_txq() took it for served already and ended
the round without handing out anything: it doesn't look past the head.

With one station busy on an AC, every burst that fills the AQL budget
blocks the next start, so this happened on about every third refill. A
driver that stops at an empty round (mt76) then waits for its next
wake-up, a new frame or a completion; when the skipped round came from
the last completion, the frames left waited for unrelated traffic or the
sender's retransmission timer.

Keep the running count in last_schedule_round and leave 0 to mean
"blocked", which is all ieee80211_next_txq() reads it for.

---
--- a/net/mac80211/ieee80211_i.h
+++ b/net/mac80211/ieee80211_i.h
@@ -1421,6 +1421,7 @@ struct ieee80211_local {
 	spinlock_t active_txq_lock[IEEE80211_NUM_ACS];
 	struct list_head active_txqs[IEEE80211_NUM_ACS];
 	u16 schedule_round[IEEE80211_NUM_ACS];
+	u16 last_schedule_round[IEEE80211_NUM_ACS];
 
 	/* serializes ieee80211_handle_wake_tx_queue */
 	spinlock_t handle_wake_tx_queue_lock;
--- a/net/mac80211/tx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/tx.c
@@ -4326,9 +4326,16 @@ void ieee80211_txq_schedule_start(struct ieee80211_hw 
 	spin_lock_bh(&local->active_txq_lock[ac]);
 
 	if (ieee80211_txq_schedule_airtime_check(local, ac)) {
-		local->schedule_round[ac]++;
+		/*
+		 * Count on from the last round that ran: restarting at 1
+		 * after a round the AC's limit blocked (0) would match the
+		 * round a txq was last served in, and next_txq() would take
+		 * it for served already and end the round without serving
+		 * anyone.
+		 */
+		local->schedule_round[ac] = ++local->last_schedule_round[ac];
 		if (!local->schedule_round[ac])
-			local->schedule_round[ac]++;
+			local->schedule_round[ac] = ++local->last_schedule_round[ac];
 	} else {
 		local->schedule_round[ac] = 0;
 	}
